From ecd022dca938aa5cec4b7ca05dea62f862bd2248 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Young <git@ryanyoung.io>
Date: Fri, 1 May 2026 01:11:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Recover self-context (paneId + TMUX env) when launched
 without TMUX_PANE
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When the bridge is spawned as a subprocess by an MCP client that
doesn't propagate $TMUX_PANE (notably Codex CLI's MCP launcher, but
applies to any spawner that doesn't explicitly forward tmux env vars),
two cascading bugs surface:

  Bridge-A: tmux_id() throws "Not running inside a tmux pane
            ($TMUX_PANE is unset)" instead of recovering.
  Bridge-B: tmux_message() emits headers like
            "[tmux-bridge from:unknown pane:unknown id:<8hex>]"
            because it falls back to the literal string "unknown" when
            process.env.TMUX_PANE is empty.

Both were observable live in codex-pair on 2026-04-26. Codex worked
around them by walking tmux_list() output to identify itself, but
every MCP consumer of the bridge has to re-derive that workaround.

Fix
---
Add a getSelfContext() helper that recovers both the pane ID *and*
the TMUX env (so detectSocketArgs() targets the right server, not
just the right pane). Three-tier resolution:

  1. Fast path: process.env.TMUX_PANE / process.env.TMUX (current
     behavior).
  2. Walk parent process tree unbounded (until pid 1 / 0 / cycle),
     collecting ancestor PIDs. For each ancestor read its env via
     /proc/<pid>/environ (Linux) or `ps eww -p <pid>` (macOS / BSD).
     Return the first ancestor with TMUX_PANE set.
  3. Final fallback: query `tmux list-panes -a -F '#{pane_pid}
     #{pane_id}'` and match collected ancestor PIDs against pane PIDs.
     Socket args remain unrecovered in this branch (we couldn't recover
     TMUX env, so we use the default socket — log a warning).

The result is cached at module scope so repeated tmux invocations
don't re-walk the process tree.

Threading
---------
Three callsites consumed bare process.env.TMUX_PANE:

  - id() (returned the env value or threw).
  - message() (used "unknown" as a fallback for the from:/pane: header).
  - assertNotSelf() (loop-prevention check; silently disabled when env
    was unset).

assertNotSelf() stays sync; signature changed from
  (paneId, action) => (targetPaneId, selfPaneId, action)
so callers (type/message/keys) resolve self-context once at the top
and pass selfPaneId in. message() additionally uses the recovered
context for its from:/pane: header, eliminating the "unknown" literal.

tmux() now warms the self-context cache before each call so
detectSocketArgs() automatically picks up any recovered TMUX env.
A private rawTmux() helper exists to break the bootstrap recursion
in computeSelfContext()'s fallback (it can't depend on socket
detection — that's the thing it's trying to recover).

Tests
-----
- Unit tests for assertNotSelf cover the four scenarios threading
  exposes (target==self for message/type, target!=self, self===undefined).
- Unit tests for getSelfContext cover the env-set fast path and the
  cache memoization invariant.
- New integration test (env-scrub.test.ts) spawns a node subprocess
  inside the test runner's tmux pane with TMUX/TMUX_PANE cleared
  and asserts:
    (a) getSelfContext() returns a concrete %N (not throwing),
    (b) the recovered context includes the parent's TMUX env,
    (c) the recovered paneId is never the literal "unknown".
  Skipped when the test process is not itself running inside a tmux
  pane (test infra dependency, not a logic dependency).

Other
-----
- Bumped MCP server version literal in src/index.ts (was 0.1.0,
  out-of-sync with package.json which is now 0.3.1) so clients see
  consistent version signals.
- doctor() now reports recovered self-context when env was unset,
  so users can see whether and via which path recovery succeeded.

Verified
--------
- 61 tests pass (was 52 pre-change; +7 unit + 2 integration).
- Live verified on 2026-04-30 via codex-pair Phase 5 round-trip:
  bridge subprocess spawned by Codex with empty TMUX_PANE successfully
  recovers and emits headers with concrete pane:%N values.
